{
  "_": "The lane manifest (B-163, docs/plans/parallel-streams.md S4): docs/backlog.md §'Parallel lanes' as data. `lanes` maps each lane letter of the lane table to the files it may edit, as globs (`**` spans directories, `*` one segment, `?` one character). `shared` lists the status documents every lane edits under the rule 'Status documents under streams' (B-162) — exempt from the check. A stream plan's `boundary` header narrows its lane; the plan's own file is always allowed. Lanes A, C and D were declared from the lane table's prose on 2026-10-30, K from the kernel-hygiene band of the backlog the same day; all four are refined when a stream plan opens in them; P and S come from their plans' headers. Two lanes may list the same file (P and D share the evaluator and the totality analyzer: the lane table says P takes them only when D is not in them) — the per-PR check sees one lane; overlap between ACTIVE streams is the coordinating service's check at dispatch. Edited by lane S or a maintainer decision.",
  "shared": [
    "docs/CHANGELOG.md",
    "docs/backlog.md",
    "docs/plans/README.md",
    "docs/decisions.md",
    "docs/classification.md",
    "docs/book-changes.md",
    "CLAUDE.md"
  ],
  "lanes": {
